#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:5
#: 1b77f95694ae42e8be099ddf5e467da3
msgid "V-Tail Planes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:7
#: e7506964798e42a4a10d13db82aad898
msgid "A common alternative to a traditional elevator and rudder is a V-Tail, or an ATail (an upside down V-Tail)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:10
#: e9fdb4e376494d3c8b1aca66604ce292
msgid "A V-Tail aircraft has the same functionality as a standard aircraft, but it requires special configuration of the servo outputs. Do not use V-Tail mixing on the transmitter. Although you may choose custom channels, the typical V-Tail setup uses channel 2 and 4 for the servo outputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:16
#: a86891ebf6e249bbb3f335b610add0fe
msgid "Remove the propeller from the aircraft before starting the setup process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:20
#: 9f347d57768049a7b2a8ebafa50e3adf
msgid "Configuration & Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:22
#: b4d7022db6c1428d9641c42bcbb0fc79
msgid "The most important step to setting up the plane is having the correct inputs, outputs, and reversals. Inputs are covered on the :ref:`RC input setup page <rc-throw-trim>`. After the RC inputs are configured, configure the outputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:26
#: 2b0c5865680149c78c1cab7a0266d3dd
msgid "Make sure the :ref:`AHRS_ORIENTATION<AHRS_ORIENTATION>` is set correctly for the autopilot. If it is incorrect, this setup will fail, and the plane may crash upon entry into any stabilize mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:29
#: 4b2067aa333e4e1aa0ba69719e7cf35d
msgid "Servo cables can be connected to any output of the autopilot, but using the default channels 1-4 listed below is recommended. Set the SERVOn_FUNCTIONS to the appropriate values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:45
#: a6d348026e4a40e1a6cedad8c90fe12b
msgid "Servo Function & Reversal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:47
#: 3157db7c2c7e4e1f99277e542f41cbac
msgid "The next step is to correct the V-Tail functions and reversals. Both the function and reversal go hand-in-hand, so modifying one may partially change the behavior of the other. Connect the battery (with propeller removed) and turn on the RC transmitter. Switch to FBWA mode using the function switch or a ground station command, and disable the safety switch (if fitted)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:54
#: 4197fb07f383460cae944625e436dd53
msgid "When the plane is level, the servos should be near their trim values. Move the plane and leave the transmitter sticks centered while monitoring the control surfaces to determine if the function and reversals are correct. See the table for the correct control surface response to the movements. In each instance, the plane should move its control surfaces to level itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:73
#: a7b8882dd0284850bf8fc65e85f0f2f8
msgid "If the ailerons do not respond correctly, reverse the output by changing the corresponding SERVOn_REVERSED setting (from 0 to 1, or from 1 to 0)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:76
#: 46cdcf5b81104e878bd12d127e326a9e
msgid "If the V-tails do not respond correctly, change parameters using the following table to enable the correct behavior. Work on one channel at a time to avoid confusion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:88
#: 888bd726bf3e41d7978034204083bf53
msgid ":ref:`KFF_RDDRMIX<KFF_RDDRMIX>` must not be set to 0 for rudder setup. If the plane actually needs 0, then reset it after this setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:91
#: 182b8b1ff4f74010b8e45fc32110d04c
msgid ":ref:`KFF_RDDRMIX<KFF_RDDRMIX>` should cause the tail surfaces point in the direction of the raised aileron."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:96
#: 26c0987da4e34a40ad424818dd239be9
msgid "Confirm RC Transmitter Input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:98
#: f0d60782925644259f2cdf20b453e449
msgid "Keep the plane level in FBWA mode and command the following inputs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:112
#: 238c4db11b774cb1b8661b6a04814261
msgid "Double check MANUAL mode for the inputs as well. If everything is setup correctly, the plane should be almost ready to fly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:116
#: b8f76ad8bb9d404a8dd2fa239e3815c9
msgid "ATail Planes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:118
#: 3de36b4bc5ba41ae8de2a8eeb428c601
msgid "With \"A-Tail\" planes (an inverted V-Tail), the control surface movements referenced above should still be the same directions. It is likely that the servo reversal or function will be opposite from a similar V-Tail setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:123
#: d51fb2fc216e4ab2aaff01e6657a85a0
msgid "Servo Trim"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:125
#: ed1fb1ade0f94882936663118893ad41
msgid "Switch back to MANUAL mode in order to adjust the servo trim values. The servo trim is in the SERVOn_TRIM parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:128
#: 3f05a4d9745d4889b2b82725b4aae1a2
msgid "Adjust the trim values so that the servo is centered when the transmitter sticks are centered. If the trim value is not between 1450 and 1550 PWM, mechanical trim adjustment is recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:133
#: 88a93f2cb71744fcb0564b7965ad5e77
msgid "Servo Throw"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:135
#: ae7b0a2b423d4051b8005f7eb46ef0d0
msgid "Finally adjust the servo throws (range of movement for each of the servos)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:138
#: 7daa2c68d9e240a0834a57280bdb9b3c
msgid "Check any instructions that came with the plane for suggested throw values. These are often specified in millimeters or inches of movement of the trailing edge of the control surface close to the fuselage. If suggested throw values are not found, then choose a throw that doesn't cause the servos to \"bind\" (often indicated by a high pitched sound when servos stall)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:145
#: 06c84d91a4e84812be88215287f5b32b
msgid "To adjust the throw, change the SERVOn_MIN and SERVOn_MAX values. The defaults are 1100 to 1900. On many aircraft, more throw may be desired. Changing throws to 1000 to 2000 or beyond is normal. Make sure that the servos are still moving when nearing the extreme values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:150
#: e2d6b1db74a0463990aab24b6cffdc81
msgid "To get to maximum throw on V-Tail control surfaces, command pitch and yaw at the same time in MANUAL mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:154
#: a0050dc0c2874a5c870b309891292646
msgid "Mixing Gain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:156
#: 0b285c21606e404cbbc0ab024627a5c6
msgid "The :ref:`MIXING_GAIN<MIXING_GAIN>` parameter is critical for vtail aircraft. It is the gain used in mixing between yaw and pitch output and the vtail movement. For example, if :ref:`MIXING_GAIN<MIXING_GAIN>` is 0.5, then the following outputs are used:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:161
#: ae3a850dc5c0460aa3c913ae79d69e22
msgid "LEFT_VTAIL = (yaw+pitch)*0.5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:162
#: b6849e21253843cb89bddbe01ef61dc0
msgid "RIGHT_VTAIL = (-yaw+pitch)*0.5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:164
#: e696da58797947f4b0f72779c3bf7b34
msgid "Adjusting the :ref:`MIXING_GAIN<MIXING_GAIN>` controls the percentage of throws from pitch vs yaw."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:167
#: 9edbf59e774b4fff851ce715159185f6
msgid "Final Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-vtail-plane.rst:169
#: 852fcd74fc68441bae1ba3f0a5c110a3
msgid "After completing the V-Tail guide, move onto the final setup of the aircraft."
msgstr ""

